1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,020
Ibn Mas‘ud entered upon his wife and saw something around her neck.

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:05,140
What did he do?

3
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:11,200
Zaynab, the wife of ‘Abdullah ibn Mas‘ud (may Allah be pleased with them both), had hung a thread around her neck

4
00:00:11,510 --> 00:00:13,240
because her eye was hurting her,

5
00:00:13,570 --> 00:00:15,270
and she thought it would help her.

6
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:18,480
When ‘Abdullah saw it, he cut it off and said:

7
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:21,580
“The family of ‘Abdullah have no need of shirk.

8
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:25,090
I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say:

9
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:28,210
‘Indeed, spells, amulets and love charms are shirk.’”

10
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:29,810
(Narrated by Abu Dawud)

11
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:30,920
What is meant

12
00:00:31,350 --> 00:00:35,180
is ruqyah that contains shirk. As for ruqyah with the Qur’an, it is permitted.

13
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:39,390
So do not hang beads, threads, or anything else to ward off the evil eye.

14
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:43,510
Protection comes through dhikr and reliance on Allah alone.

15
00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:47,800
Share this clip with someone you love, and follow the channel.

